  "goodToKnow": "Die Larve is a larva: Insektenlarven, die Mückenlarve. A caterpillar is die Raupe, and a pupa die Puppe (also doll). Originally, Larve meant mask or ghost, from Latin larva, and in Swiss and southern German carnival (Fasnacht), the carved wooden masks are still called Larven. The v is pronounced as f: LAR-fe. Plural: die Larven."
